N2  - The proceedings contain 19 papers. The topics discussed include: proposal of a new prognostic clinicopathological classification of pituitary endocrine tumors; biomarkers of pituitary neoplasms; treatment of aggressive pituitary tumors with temozolomide. an update; advances in navigation for pituitary surgery; pituitary surgery beyond the sella; plurihormonality and pluripotentiality of GH-secreting adenoma based on pathological analysis of 242 patients with acromegaly; transsphenoidal microsurgical results of female patients with prolactinomas; silent corticotroph adenomas: an update; characterization of pituitary adenomas by mass spectrometry based proteomics; clinical, morphological, immunohistochemical and ultrastructural study of a mixed pituitary adenoma/craniopharyngioma; update in pathology of nonfunctioning pituitary adenomas; the impact of igf-1R and VEGF on cellular proliferation and invasiveness of pituitary adenomas; controversial diagnosis in pituitary pathology: atypical and invasive adenomas; recurrences of pituitary adenomas: comparisons with first tumours; and aggressive pituitary adenomas.
